{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786561701304,"sessionID":"ses_008a7474dffeDMoYnQ74TeMyw4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_0k0v87VkSpSA31hXxicd8645","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-diagram && echo \"=== 'SKILL.md §' section refs ===\"; grep -rhoE 'SKILL\\.md §[0-9]+[–-][0-9]+|SKILL\\.md §[0-9]+' . --include='*.md' --include='*.yaml' --include='*.txt' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; echo; echo \"=== '§9' references ===\"; grep -rl '§9' . | head -20; echo; echo \"=== '§7' / '§8' / '§0' references ===\"; grep -rl '§[078]' . | head -20"},"output":"=== 'SKILL.md §' section refs ===\n   8 SKILL.md §6\n   4 SKILL.md §9\n   1 SKILL.md §7\n   1 SKILL.md §5\n   1 SKILL.md §1\n\n=== '§9' references ===\n./references/types/type-it-state.md\n./references/types/type-high-level.md\n./references/import-export/import-mermaid.md\n./references/import-export/import-drawio.md\n./README.md\n\n=== '§7' / '§8' / '§0' references ===\n./references/types/type-sequence.md\n./references/types/type-data-flow.md\n./references/types/type-process.md\n./references/types/type-high-level.md\n./references/ascii-format/notation-and-validator.md\n./references/import-export/import-drawio.md\n","metadata":{"output":"=== 'SKILL.md §' section refs ===\n   8 SKILL.md §6\n   4 SKILL.md §9\n   1 SKILL.md §7\n   1 SKILL.md §5\n   1 SKILL.md §1\n\n=== '§9' references ===\n./references/types/type-it-state.md\n./references/types/type-high-level.md\n./references/import-export/import-mermaid.md\n./references/import-export/import-drawio.md\n./README.md\n\n=== '§7' / '§8' / '§0' references ===\n./references/types/type-sequence.md\n./references/types/type-data-flow.md\n./references/types/type-process.md\n./references/types/type-high-level.md\n./references/ascii-format/notation-and-validator.md\n./references/import-export/import-drawio.md\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-diagram && echo \"=== 'SKILL.md §' section refs ===\"; grep -rhoE 'SKILL\\.md §[0-9]+[–-][0-9]+|SKILL\\.md §[0-9]+' . --include='*.md' --include='*.yaml' --include='*.txt' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn; echo; echo \"=== '§9' references ===\"; grep -rl '§9' . | head -20; echo; echo \"=== '§7' / '§8' / '§0' references ===\"; grep -rl '§[078]' . | head -20","time":{"start":1786561701301,"end":1786561701303}},"id":"prt_ff7602101001OSDnX5NKk4mBzy","sessionID":"ses_008a7474dffeDMoYnQ74TeMyw4","messageID":"msg_ff75fa0c5001MGtYLjaNQTaHBw"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786561702290,"sessionID":"ses_008a7474dffeDMoYnQ74TeMyw4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_iUZ6W0P2j7hdzwj7d7FL8197","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-diagram && echo \"=== secrets scan ===\"; grep -rniE '(api[_-]?key|secret|password|token|bearer|BEGIN (RSA|OPENSSH|EC) PRIVATE)' . --include='*.py' --include='*.sh' --include='*.html' --include='*.md' 2>/dev/null | grep -viE 'password field|auth|no password|tokenize' | head -10; echo \"exit=$?\""},"output":"=== secrets scan ===\n./feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:48:The shared editorial design system every diagram draws against: semantic color and typography tokens, the 4px grid, the complexity budget, and the five non-negotiable connector rules.\n./feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:52:Tokens live in `references/foundations/style-guide.md` (paper, ink, muted, accent, link) with a light-dark inversion rule and a separate terminal skin; every coordinate, size, and gap must be divisible by 4; the per-diagram budget is 9 nodes, 12 arrows, 2 focal elements, and 2 callouts; connectors must use rounded orthogonal elbows, masked arrow labels with a 6-10px gap, fanned attach points, and no overlapping strokes.\n./feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:68:The gate fires only when the `accent` token is still the shipped default and offers five options (URL, skill, folder, manual tokens, default); onboarding reads the source, extracts colors and fonts, maps them to semantic roles, runs contrast checks, proposes a diff, and writes only after approval; `references/foundations/onboarding.md` documents the full flow.\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/type-selection-and-routing.md:56:| `references/foundations/style-guide.md` | Reference | Anchor for the always-loaded design-system tokens that accompany the type reference |\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:3:description: \"The shared editorial design system every diagram draws against: semantic color and typography tokens, the 4px grid, the complexity budget, and the five non-negotiable connector rules.\"\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:19:The shared editorial design system every diagram draws against: semantic color and typography tokens, the 4px grid, the complexity budget, and the five non-negotiable connector rules.\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:21:This is the visual contract behind every diagram the packet produces. Colors and typography are referred to by semantic role and resolved in `references/foundations/style-guide.md`, the single source of truth for tokens, so changing that file re-skins every future diagram without touching type-specific logic. The caller is the agent drawing the diagram, and the failure modes are the ones the taste gate catches: off-grid coordinates, over-accented focal signals, and connectors that a reader cannot trace.\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:27:### Design tokens and skins\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:29:All colors, typography, and tokens live in `references/foundations/style-guide.md` as semantic roles — `paper`, `ink`, `muted`, `accent`, `link`, and derived roles — and the hex values are looked up there rather than inlined. The default skin is a cool editorial palette (white-smoke paper, jet-black ink, atomic-tangerine accent, blue-slate muted). A light-to-dark inversion rule flips the RGB of ink-toned alpha colors, a small series palette is opt-in for the radar type only, and a separate fixed terminal skin provides the terminal-window register without being affected by onboarding. Typography is load-bearing: the page title uses Instrument Serif, human-readable names use Geist sans, technical sublabels use Geist Mono, and JetBrains Mono is never used as a blanket dev font.\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:51:| `references/foundations/style-guide.md` | Shared | Semantic token roles, typography font stack, stroke/radius/spacing tokens, node type-to-treatment mapping, and the terminal skin |\nexit=0\n","metadata":{"output":"=== secrets scan ===\n./feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:48:The shared editorial design system every diagram draws against: semantic color and typography tokens, the 4px grid, the complexity budget, and the five non-negotiable connector rules.\n./feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:52:Tokens live in `references/foundations/style-guide.md` (paper, ink, muted, accent, link) with a light-dark inversion rule and a separate terminal skin; every coordinate, size, and gap must be divisible by 4; the per-diagram budget is 9 nodes, 12 arrows, 2 focal elements, and 2 callouts; connectors must use rounded orthogonal elbows, masked arrow labels with a 6-10px gap, fanned attach points, and no overlapping strokes.\n./feature-catalog/feature-catalog.md:68:The gate fires only when the `accent` token is still the shipped default and offers five options (URL, skill, folder, manual tokens, default); onboarding reads the source, extracts colors and fonts, maps them to semantic roles, runs contrast checks, proposes a diff, and writes only after approval; `references/foundations/onboarding.md` documents the full flow.\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/type-selection-and-routing.md:56:| `references/foundations/style-guide.md` | Reference | Anchor for the always-loaded design-system tokens that accompany the type reference |\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:3:description: \"The shared editorial design system every diagram draws against: semantic color and typography tokens, the 4px grid, the complexity budget, and the five non-negotiable connector rules.\"\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:19:The shared editorial design system every diagram draws against: semantic color and typography tokens, the 4px grid, the complexity budget, and the five non-negotiable connector rules.\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:21:This is the visual contract behind every diagram the packet produces. Colors and typography are referred to by semantic role and resolved in `references/foundations/style-guide.md`, the single source of truth for tokens, so changing that file re-skins every future diagram without touching type-specific logic. The caller is the agent drawing the diagram, and the failure modes are the ones the taste gate catches: off-grid coordinates, over-accented focal signals, and connectors that a reader cannot trace.\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:27:### Design tokens and skins\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:29:All colors, typography, and tokens live in `references/foundations/style-guide.md` as semantic roles — `paper`, `ink`, `muted`, `accent`, `link`, and derived roles — and the hex values are looked up there rather than inlined. The default skin is a cool editorial palette (white-smoke paper, jet-black ink, atomic-tangerine accent, blue-slate muted). A light-to-dark inversion rule flips the RGB of ink-toned alpha colors, a small series palette is opt-in for the radar type only, and a separate fixed terminal skin provides the terminal-window register without being affected by onboarding. Typography is load-bearing: the page title uses Instrument Serif, human-readable names use Geist sans, technical sublabels use Geist Mono, and JetBrains Mono is never used as a blanket dev font.\n./feature-catalog/diagram-generation/editorial-style-and-connectors.md:51:| `references/foundations/style-guide.md` | Shared | Semantic token roles, typography font stack, stroke/radius/spacing tokens, node type-to-treatment mapping, and the terminal skin |\nexit=0\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-diagram && echo \"=== secrets scan ===\"; grep -rniE '(api[_-]?key|secret|password|token|bearer|BEGIN (RSA|OPENSSH|EC) PRIVATE)' . --include='*.py' --include='*.sh' --include='*.html' --include='*.md' 2>/dev/null | grep -viE 'password field|auth|no password|tokenize' | head -10; echo \"exit=$?\"","time":{"start":1786561702286,"end":1786561702288}},"id":"prt_ff7602587001PX6X18BwUfxqEa","sessionID":"ses_008a7474dffeDMoYnQ74TeMyw4","messageID":"msg_ff75fa0c5001MGtYLjaNQTaHBw"}}
