{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786562008310,"sessionID":"ses_008a7474dffeDMoYnQ74TeMyw4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_mYsXIxkjvlTO9AJ6BgBo4646","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-diagram && echo \"=== duplicated functions across extractors ===\"; grep -E '^def (clean_label|_has_cycle|shape_family|_fail|digest|to_json|analyze|main)\\b' scripts/drawio_extract.py scripts/mermaid_extract.py; echo; echo \"=== scripts README ===\"; head -40 scripts/README.md"},"output":"=== duplicated functions across extractors ===\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def _fail(msg: str) -> \"NoReturn\":  # type: ignore[valid-type]\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def clean_label(value: str | None) -> str:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def shape_family(shape: str) -> str:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def _has_cycle(nodes: list[Node], edges: list[Edge]) -> bool:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def analyze(page: Page) -> dict[str, Any]:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def digest(path: Path, pages: list[Page], selected: list[Page], max_rows: int) -> str:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def to_json(path: Path, pages: list[Page], selected: list[Page]) -> str:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def _fail(message: str) -> NoReturn:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def clean_label(value: str) -> str:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def _has_cycle(nodes: list[Node], edges: list[Edge]) -> bool:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def shape_family(shape: str) -> str:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def analyze(diagram: Diagram) -> dict[str, Any]:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def digest(\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def to_json(path: Path, diagrams: list[Diagram], selected: list[Diagram]) -> str:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n\n=== scripts README ===\n---\ntitle: \"sk-create-diagram scripts: Code README\"\ndescription: \"Code-facing README for the draw.io and Mermaid IR extractors plus the ASCII flowchart validator.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-create-diagram scripts\"\n  - \"drawio extractor\"\n  - \"mermaid extractor\"\n  - \"flowchart validator\"\n---\n\n# sk-create-diagram scripts\n\nThe two intermediate-representation (IR) extractors behind the import redraw flow and the validator behind the `ascii-markdown` flowchart format.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis folder owns the deterministic half of `sk-create-diagram`'s import flow: two stdlib-only Python CLIs that decode a `.drawio` or Mermaid source into a normalized IR — nodes, edges, containers, hubs, cycles, budget flags — as a compact Markdown digest (or full JSON). It also owns the shell validator required before delivering an `ascii-markdown` flowchart. Neither extractor makes a design decision; the agent reads the digest, picks a diagram type and detail level, and redraws from scratch in the packet's design system. All scripts run locally with no network access and never mutate the source file they read.\n\nBehavior details (per-type routing rules, the four output dials) live in [`../references/import-export/`](../references/import-export/) and [`../references/foundations/output-spec.md`](../references/foundations/output-spec.md); this README stays navigational.\n\n### Key Statistics\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| Code files | 3 |\n| CLI entrypoints | 3 |\n| Test suites | 0 (no committed regression suite yet) |\n\n---\n\n## 2. QUICK START\n\nRun from the packet root:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/drawio_extract.py diagram.drawio --page 1\npython3 scripts/mermaid_extract.py diagram.mmd --diagram 1\nbash scripts/validate-flowchart.sh path/to/flowchart.md\n","metadata":{"output":"=== duplicated functions across extractors ===\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def _fail(msg: str) -> \"NoReturn\":  # type: ignore[valid-type]\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def clean_label(value: str | None) -> str:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def shape_family(shape: str) -> str:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def _has_cycle(nodes: list[Node], edges: list[Edge]) -> bool:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def analyze(page: Page) -> dict[str, Any]:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def digest(path: Path, pages: list[Page], selected: list[Page], max_rows: int) -> str:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def to_json(path: Path, pages: list[Page], selected: list[Page]) -> str:\nscripts/drawio_extract.py:def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def _fail(message: str) -> NoReturn:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def clean_label(value: str) -> str:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def _has_cycle(nodes: list[Node], edges: list[Edge]) -> bool:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def shape_family(shape: str) -> str:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def analyze(diagram: Diagram) -> dict[str, Any]:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def digest(\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def to_json(path: Path, diagrams: list[Diagram], selected: list[Diagram]) -> str:\nscripts/mermaid_extract.py:def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:\n\n=== scripts README ===\n---\ntitle: \"sk-create-diagram scripts: Code README\"\ndescription: \"Code-facing README for the draw.io and Mermaid IR extractors plus the ASCII flowchart validator.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"sk-create-diagram scripts\"\n  - \"drawio extractor\"\n  - \"mermaid extractor\"\n  - \"flowchart validator\"\n---\n\n# sk-create-diagram scripts\n\nThe two intermediate-representation (IR) extractors behind the import redraw flow and the validator behind the `ascii-markdown` flowchart format.\n\n---\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\nThis folder owns the deterministic half of `sk-create-diagram`'s import flow: two stdlib-only Python CLIs that decode a `.drawio` or Mermaid source into a normalized IR — nodes, edges, containers, hubs, cycles, budget flags — as a compact Markdown digest (or full JSON). It also owns the shell validator required before delivering an `ascii-markdown` flowchart. Neither extractor makes a design decision; the agent reads the digest, picks a diagram type and detail level, and redraws from scratch in the packet's design system. All scripts run locally with no network access and never mutate the source file they read.\n\nBehavior details (per-type routing rules, the four output dials) live in [`../references/import-export/`](../references/import-export/) and [`../references/foundations/output-spec.md`](../references/foundations/output-spec.md); this README stays navigational.\n\n### Key Statistics\n\n| Metric | Value |\n|---|---:|\n| Code files | 3 |\n| CLI entrypoints | 3 |\n| Test suites | 0 (no committed regression suite yet) |\n\n---\n\n## 2. QUICK START\n\nRun from the packet root:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/drawio_extract.py diagram.drawio --page 1\npython3 scripts/mermaid_extract.py diagram.mmd --diagram 1\nbash scripts/validate-flowchart.sh path/to/flowchart.md\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd .opencode/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-diagram && echo \"=== duplicated functions across extractors ===\"; grep -E '^def (clean_label|_has_cycle|shape_family|_fail|digest|to_json|analyze|main)\\b' scripts/drawio_extract.py scripts/mermaid_extract.py; echo; echo \"=== scripts README ===\"; head -40 scripts/README.md","time":{"start":1786562008308,"end":1786562008310}},"id":"prt_ff764d27b00181nHZkeDEY87wB","sessionID":"ses_008a7474dffeDMoYnQ74TeMyw4","messageID":"msg_ff764b103001lT6d59d6fG2E9f"}}
